This implementation assumes that the input arrays do not contain duplicate elements, so no additional checks are needed. If duplicates are allowed, you'll need to either remove them before calling this function or add logic to handle multiple occurrences of common elements.

Keep in mind that this method has a time complexity of O(n^2) in the worst case scenario when no common elements exist between the arrays. For large arrays, consider using hash tables or sorting techniques for more efficient common element detection. However, in small cases like the given example, this naive approach should be sufficient.
